  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Slaked lime is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ca</mi><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, when it pass through carbon dioxide it form&nbsp;calcium carbonate, but in presence of excess carbon dioxide it forms calcium bicarbonate.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Slaked</mi><mo>lime</mo><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Pass</mi></munderover><mi>CaC</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8595;</mo></mrow><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext>Prolonged&#160;passage&#160;of</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></munderover><mi>Ca</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>HCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p>",
